# TODO - Annotated Malbolge source syntax and formatter

## Objective

Add an explicit readable Malbolge source form that supports multiline layout,
full-line comments, deterministic automatic formatting, and source maps while
canonicalizing to exactly the same position-sensitive `.malbolge` bytes consumed
by the selected profile loader.

## Acceptance

- Raw canonical `.malbolge` remains unchanged: whitespace is ignored as today,
  and `#` has no implicit comment meaning in the canonical format.
- Annotated v1 recognizes `#` as a full-line comment marker only when it is the
  first non-whitespace byte and is followed by horizontal space or tab. Bare
  hash, hash before line ending/end of file, `#X`, and inline hashes remain
  code.
- Canonicalization strips ASCII whitespace/comments and then invokes the exact
  selected-profile loader, so presentation cannot bypass source validation.
- A deterministic formatter inserts automatic line breaks without changing any
  loaded position and never emits an accidental full-line comment marker from
  code bytes.
- Compiler/decompiler integrations may align comments and breaks with C/IR
  regions and preserve an annotated-to-canonical source map.
- The active safe-Rust frontend already exposes canonical bytes plus exact
  annotated offset/line/column mappings, deterministic automatic wrapping, and
  explicit constructors on `Machine`, `ExecutionMachine`, and `ProfileMachine`.
  Existing canonical constructors remain unchanged.
- Round-trip tests prove `canonicalize(format(canonical)) == canonical`
  byte-for-byte across slash-heavy, whitespace-heavy, classic, and
  current-profile
  fixtures.
- LF, CRLF, and CR presentations canonicalize identically, and parsing is
  locale-independent.
- Evidence is durable enough to retire this TODO without losing the
  raw/canonical
  compatibility boundary.

## Evidence

- Expected durable artifact surface: `tools/`, `compiler/`, `src/`, `tests/`,
  `docs/technical/tooling/annotated-malbolge-source-format.md`.
- Current evidence: `tests/vm/annotated.rs` has seven strict fixtures covering
  hash/comment ambiguity, LF/CRLF/CR, source-map positions, invalid bytes,
  automatic-wrap round trips, loader fail-closed behavior, and classic/facade/
  current-profile execution equivalence.
- Remaining evidence: compiler/decompiler C/IR-aligned structural annotations
  and
  source-map composition against real emitted layout.
- Prerequisite completion evidence: `canonical-malbolge-target-profile`,
  `safe-rust-malbolge-vm`, `malbolge-layout-and-encoding-backend`.

